The root Go module contains no third-party code: the Go standard library is its only dependency.

mcp/ (rhobound-mcp, the MCP server) is a separate Go module. It vendors no third-party code, but it depends on, and
its binaries include, the Go modules listed with their licences in mcp/THIRD-PARTY.md: the official MCP Go SDK
(github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk, Apache-2.0 and MIT, as its LICENSE states), github.com/google/jsonschema-go
(MIT), github.com/segmentio/asm and github.com/segmentio/encoding (MIT; segmentio/encoding includes code from the Go
standard library under the Go Authors' BSD-style licence), github.com/yosida95/uritemplate/v3 (BSD-3-Clause) and
golang.org/x/oauth2, golang.org/x/sync, golang.org/x/sys and golang.org/x/time (BSD-3-Clause).

The root module does contain third-party data: internal/infer/testdata/counts/, internal/infer/testdata/hops/browse-45s/
and internal/infer/testdata/nested/ hold cut-down excerpts of traces produced by the OpenTelemetry Demo
(https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-demo, release 2.2.0, whose Kubernetes manifest runs the Demo's 2.1.3
service images), Copyright The OpenTelemetry Authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; internal/infer/testdata/README.md says what was kept. validation/cluster/
downloads the Demo's Kubernetes manifest when it runs and does not contain it.

rust/ (rbfast, an optional Rust port of the Go binary) contains code derived from the Go standard library,
Copyright The Go Authors, under the BSD-3-Clause licence in rust/LICENSE-GO; each such file names the Go file it is
derived from. Some of it (Exp, Log, Lgamma, Erfc) comes through Go from FreeBSD's msun, Copyright (C) 1993 and 2004
by Sun Microsystems, Inc., whose notices are kept in rust/crates/math/src/gomath.rs. rust/ depends on the
third-party crates listed, with their licences, in rust/THIRD-PARTY.md.
